---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: 'Privacy Policy — Minde Technologies GmbH',
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-12 text-default sm:py-16 lg:py-20">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl mb-4">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted mb-8">Last updated: August 2026</p>

    <div class="space-y-6 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-default mb-2">1. Controller and Overview</h2>
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy outlines how <strong>Minde Technologies GmbH</strong> ("we", "us", or "our") collects, 
          processes, and protects personal data in compliance with the Swiss Federal Act on Data Protection (revDSG / FADP) 
          and, where applicable, the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).
        </p>
        <div class="mt-3 p-4 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800 text-sm">
          <p><strong>Minde Technologies GmbH</strong></p>
          <p>Mülistrasse 5, 8320 Fehraltorf, Switzerland</p>
          <p>Email: <a href="mailto:business@mindetech.ch" class="text-primary hover:underline">business@mindetech.ch</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-default mb-2">2. Data We Collect</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>Technical Data:</strong> IP address, browser type, operating system, access timestamps, and referring URLs collected automatically via web server logs to ensure network security and uptime.</li>
          <li><strong>Contact and Inquiry Data:</strong> Name, business email, company name, phone number, and message content submitted when reaching out to us via email or contact forms regarding our ICT, robotics, or cross-border consulting services.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-default mb-2">3. Purpose and Legal Basis of Processing</h2>
        <p>We process your data exclusively for the following purposes:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 mt-2">
          <li>To operate, maintain, and secure our corporate website.</li>
          <li>To respond to customer requests, provide technical consulting, and execute pre-contractual negotiations.</li>
          <li>To fulfill statutory accounting and commercial obligations in Switzerland.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-default mb-2">4. Cookies and Web Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          Our website prioritizes data minimization. We only use essential technical cookies strictly necessary for core functionality and theme preferences (e.g., light/dark mode). We do not deploy intrusive third-party cross-site behavioral tracking cookies without prior explicit consent.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-default mb-2">5. Cross-Border Data Transfer</h2>
        <p>
          As an enterprise bridging European and international technology sectors, your technical or business inquiries may be handled by authorized personnel or cloud infrastructure located within Switzerland or the European Economic Area (EEA). If data transfer outside these regions is necessary, it is conducted under standard contractual clauses (SCCs) or verified adequacy decisions ensuring equivalent data protection levels under Swiss law.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-default mb-2">6. Data Retention and Security</h2>
        <p>
          We retain personal data only as long as required to achieve the processing purpose or comply with statutory retention laws (e.g., commercial and tax records retained up to 10 years). We implement appropriate technical and organizational measures (including TLS/HTTPS encryption) to prevent unauthorized access or disclosure.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-default mb-2">7. Your Statutory Rights</h2>
        <p>Under the Swiss FADP and GDPR, you possess the right to:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 mt-2">
          <li>Request access to your stored personal data.</li>
          <li>Request rectification of incorrect or incomplete data.</li>
          <li>Request erasure or restriction of processing where legally applicable.</li>
          <li>Lodge a complaint with the competent supervisory authority (in Switzerland: the Federal Data Protection and Information Commissioner, FDPIC / EDÖB).</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2">
          For inquiries or rights requests, contact us directly at <a href="mailto:business@mindetech.ch" class="text-primary hover:underline">business@mindetech.ch</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
